    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 298\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nSenate Bill Number 5421-A, entitled:\n\n    \"AN ACT relating to capital acquisition funds maintained by regional\n      off-track betting corporations\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This  bill  would allow regional off-track betting corporations (OTBs)\nto annually spend up to $500,000  of  their  capital  acquisition  funds\n(CAF) for general operating purposes, and to do so in perpetuity.\n\n  This  legislation  is fundamentally flawed. The Legislature authorized\noff-track pari-mutuel betting with the primary purpose \"to  derive  from\nsuch betting ... a reasonable revenue for the support of government.\" It\nauthorized the creation of CAFs \"for the purpose of financing the acqui-\nsition,  construction or equipping of offices, facilities or premises of\nthe corporation,\" and  allowed  the  CAFs  to  be  funded  by  diverting\nsurcharge  revenues  that  otherwise  would  have  been payable to local\ngovernments.\n\n  This bill would undermine the purpose of CAFs -- to enhance  corporate\npremises  with the aim of attracting additional bettors. With no sunset,\nthe bill would allow for the slow depletion of CAF  monies  intended  to\nimprove  the OTB operations, without addressing the real problem hurting\nOTBs financially, a statutory formula that forces OTBs to make unafford-\nable payments to racetracks, most of which now support with  own  finan-\ncial  position  with  large  revenue streams from the operation of video\nlottery terminals.\n\n  Before repurposing CAF funds, the racing industry must  come  together\nand  restructure  the statutory funding formula driving the distribution\nof handle among racing entities. I am directing my staff  to  facilitate\nthat process, and vetoing this legislation.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 298,
